GradeEditorial sets a short path (a grid block of about five items) as an editorial spread: the heading oversized on a navy mast, a geometric pipe collage facing asymmetric fact blocks whose key words (a grade, a span, a figure) are set huge.

- Look: `"look": "grade-editorial"` on a `grid` block (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-grade-editorial.js`). Items keep `{t, d, link}`; the title carries the link. Optional display fields, shown instead of `d` when present: `big` `[{v, pre, l}]` (a word or figure set huge, a small word before it, its label under it), `span` `[from, to]` (a drawn run from one end of the scope to the other), `list` `[lines]` (a breakdown on leader rules off one spine; after a `span`, a plain mono list), `bars` `[labels]` with `bars_note` (small bars whose values are still to come: dashed empty tracks and the placeholder under them), `kicker` (a line above the list), `panel: true` (the block sits on navy, its list numbered). Keep `d` as the full sentence (other renderers use it); the display fields only re-cut its words.
- Markup: `section.aq-band--limestone.aq-grade-editorial-band` > `.aq-grade-editorial__mast` (the section head on full-bleed navy) and `.aq-grade-editorial` > `figure.aq-grade-editorial__art` (aria-hidden collage svg) + `.aq-grade-editorial__grid` of `.aq-grade-editorial__item`.
- Layout: art 5 of 12 columns; the grid's six sub-columns take the first two items 3 + 3 and the next three 2 + 2 + 2 (five items; other counts run 3 + 3). With two items or fewer (industries.5) the art is cropped on desktop to a whole-row band, tile rows 1-4 of the 80-unit grid at 3:2 (about 487 × 325 at 1280; pass 12 round C), so no tile row is cut mid-way, the pipe enters at the top edge and leaves at the bottom, and the art no longer stands far past the blocks.
- Colours: `limestone` ground (light in both themes), `navy` and `on-navy` tiles, a 16 % navy tint, the hollow pipe in `navy` walls over `limestone`, water in `flow` mixed 60 % with `navy`. Text `on-limestone` / `on-limestone-muted`; the panel `on-navy`. Placeholders stay chips.
- Phones: mast, the collage as a full-width 4:3 band cropped through its middle (pass 12), then one block per row; big words at 64 / 48 px; the grade and plain-terms links carry 44 px targets.
- Not for long items: each block carries a few words; sentences belong in LinkGrid.

Motion (`motion.js`): the collage tiles drop into the grid from scattered quarter turns, the pipe walls draw, the tank and pump seat over them, the water runs the route once and the drop falls; the blocks wipe in one by one, titles decode, big words rise letter by letter from a mask, the scope run draws across, list lines slide out, the empty bar tracks draw on and the navy panel wipes up (about 3.8 s). Nothing under reduced motion.

**Dark (pass 12 round C, RC1).** The limestone band turns warm stone in dark; the display values (`__v`) and the span
(`__span`) take `--on-limestone` there, because navy on stone is about 1.2:1. Light mode is unchanged.
